      "exact_witness_family": "For every M,k>=1, n_(M,k)=4Mk-1 has v2(3n+1)=1 and T(n)=6Mk-1. Both values are -1 mod M and T(n)-n=2Mk>0.",
      "no_go_proof": "On the residue r=-1 mod M, lower boundedness along arbitrarily large n forces a_r>=0. If a_r=0, R(T(n))=R(n); if a_r>0, R(T(n))-R(n)=2Mk*a_r>0. Strict one-step descent is impossible.",
